### P1 — “Vacuous pass” remains possible

`guards_broken` is syntactically validated but never matched to the transcript:

- Capture runs any operator-supplied command and records only output/exit metadata: [bin/coverloop:977](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:977).
- The claimed count is added separately after capture/attachment: [bin/coverloop:1373](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1373), [bin/coverloop:1387](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1387).
- Attached evidence needs only nonempty text; its contents are not interpreted: [bin/coverloop:1083](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1083).
- Verification checks source, exit code, path, hash, and nonempty output—but not mutant identities/results or their relationship to `guards_broken`: [bin/coverloop:1501](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1501), [bin/coverloop:1552](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/bin/coverloop:1552).
- Default gating explicitly accepts self-attested mutation evidence: [tests/test_gate.py:879](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/tests/test_gate.py:879).

Therefore an L3 report can pass:

- Normally: `--mutation pass --mutation-guards 1`, with no transcript.
- With `--require-transcript`: attach any nonempty text.
- With `--require-executed`: run an exit-zero command producing any nonempty output, such as `printf done`.

This is partly acknowledged by the general attester-authored trust ceiling, but it means v2.12.1 does not operationally close the vacuous-pass gap it claims to close at [docs/DESIGN-NOTE-v2.12.md:68](/Users/[REDACTED:user]/code/coverloop/docs/DESIGN-NOTE-v2.12.md:68).

